  <diagram name="Scope and Findings" id="w05-findings">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#183c43;align=left;" value="Week 5 | Scope and Findings" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1070" x="45" y="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="scope" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=12;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;font&gt;&lt;b&gt;1 · Process scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;Craig Temple.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;This process shows the flow of how an appointment moves from booking to intake. It starts when a visitor request an appointment. It ends when Intake passes to the next staff team.&amp;nbsp;The roles include Visitor, Scheduling, Clinical Operations, Intake, and the next staff team. Anything after the handoff, such as treatment, is outside the scope.The roles include Visitor, Scheduling, Clinical Operations, Intake, and the next staff team. Anything after the handoff, such as treatment, is outside the scope.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="1070" x="45" y="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="walkthrough" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · Check the two paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;For a normal appointment, the visitor requests a time, Scheduling records the details, and Clinical Operations checks availability. If ready, Intake confirms support arrangements and passes the visitor forward.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;For the incident, the visitor received a booking confirmation, but Intake still showed held when they arrived. W05-S04 does not show a completed readiness decision before arrival. This does not prove the decision never happened, only that it is missing from the available records.For a normal appointment, the visitor requests a time, Scheduling records the details, and Clinical Operations checks availability. If ready, Intake confirms support arrangements and passes the visitor forward.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;For the incident, the visitor received a booking confirmation, but Intake still showed held when they arrived. W05-S04 does not show a completed readiness decision before arrival. This does not prove the decision never happened, only that it is missing from the available records.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="215" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · Evidence and model review&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;W05-S01 supports the booking and Scheduling steps. W05-S02 supports the readiness decision and held status. W05-S03 supports Intake&#39;s ready and held paths. W05-S04 supports the incident and missing handoff.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;After reviewing the records, I made sure the model separates booking confirmation from clinical readiness and includes both held paths. The remaining uncertainty is how the readiness decision reaches Intake. I would need clarification from Clinical Operations, Intake, or the missing readiness record. No stakeholder approval has been confirmed.W05-S01 supports the booking and Scheduling steps. W05-S02 supports the readiness decision and held status. W05-S03 supports Intake&#39;s ready and held paths. W05-S04 supports the incident and missing handoff.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;After reviewing the records, I made sure the model separates booking confirmation from clinical readiness and includes both held paths. The remaining uncertainty is how the readiness decision reaches Intake. I would need clarification from Clinical Operations, Intake, or the missing readiness record. No stakeholder approval has been confirmed.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="reflection" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;4 · Learning reflection (reuse your Discord paragraph)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;This model made it clearer that just because an appointment is “booked” does not mean it is ready for a visitor to be seen by the next staff team. Clinical ops decides the readiness of the visitor, while intake checks the status when the visitor arrives. The handoff of readiness to intake is unclear in W05-S04 because the trace doesn’t show a completed decision before patient arrival. Unlike Week 4, which was writing down details in theory, week 5 provided a visual representation of the current process in practice.&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="525" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="evidence" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=14;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;5 · Portfolio evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;[Editable model filename and Week05/Evidence/Week05_Discord_Post.png or .jpg. If Discord is unavailable, identify the equivalent reflection used here.]&lt;br&gt;Save the .drawio file; export both pages as one PDF; check readability; commit and push." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="1070" x="45" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
